Third-party code in src/
------------------------

An auxiliary hashtable derived from the 1994 JDK carries an embedded Sun
Microsystems notice permitting use for NON-COMMERCIAL purposes only. The
derived code is one package-private class in each of two files:

    src/zeta/agl/HashMap.java   final class HashMapTab
    src/zeta/agl/HashSet.java   final class HashSetTab

That notice is narrower than the Apache License and is not superseded by it,
so commercial redistribution of ZETA requires replacing those two classes.
Neither is public and nothing outside its own file names it -- but the
replacement is not a drop-in: these classes decide hash-bucket iteration
order, which is observable in ZETA's output, so a replacement that does not
reproduce the same order changes rendered text and every affected regression
baseline has to be re-recorded deliberately.

src/zeta/agl/Option.java is attributed to Martin Odersky and derives from the
Pizza 1.0 standard library (1996).


